  <!-- SLIDE 8: Teacher's Note / Error Correction -->
  <cosy-slide id="slide-5" stage="error-correction" duration="50" mode="all">
    <cosy-teacher-notes type="additional">
      <p><cosy-text type="strong">Teacher&apos;s Linguistic Error Correction Guidance:</cosy-text></p>
      <ul>
        <li>Incorrect: I was sympathizing with her struggles → Correct: I was empathizing with her struggles / showed deep empathy ((Linguistic register: &apos;sympathize&apos; suggests feeling pity, while &apos;empathize&apos; implies a deeper psychological understanding and shared feelings))</li>
        <li>Incorrect: We discussed about the psychological impact → Correct: We discussed the psychological impact / had a discussion about the psychological impact ((Underlined prepositional error. Better collocation: &apos;discuss&apos; is transitive and takes no preposition, or use &apos;have a discussion about&apos;))</li>
        <li>Incorrect: This habit is deeply ingrowed in our brain → Correct: This habit is deeply ingrained / embedded in our subconscious ((Collocation: &apos;ingrained&apos; or &apos;embedded&apos; are the correct advanced adjectives for psychological/behavioural patterns))</li>
      </ul>
    </cosy-teacher-notes>
